# Zig build outputs.  Appended by the Zig packaging; every upstream entry
# above is preserved unchanged.  These are the two directories `zig build`
# creates by default in Zig 0.16.  The patterns carry no leading slash, so
# they also cover consumer/, which is a package in its own right.  An
# operator who redirects the cache with --cache-dir owns that path.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# Zig 0.16 materialises an archive-fetched dependency beside the build root
# that asked for it (AGENTS.md section 6), so it is a working-tree
# artefact like .zig-cache/ and not a package path.  consumer/ gets its own
# copy by the same rule; the patterns carry no leading slash.
zig-pkg/

# `--prefix` sends the install tree somewhere else entirely, but a build
# that installs into its own root (or a runner invoked with an explicit
# destination) leaves `result` symlinks behind.  Both names, never a
# leading slash, so they also match under consumer/.
result
result-*
